<title>USA: AES Corp raises $184 mln for UK power plant.</title>
<headline>AES Corp raises $184 mln for UK power plant.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>AES Corp said Friday that it raised $184 million of non-recourse project finance for its 230 megawatt (MW) gas-fired combined cycle power plant in Barry, South Wales, United Kingdom.</p>
<p>The credit facility is underwritten by Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd , said AES.  It is the first project in the United Kingdom to be project financed without any of the electric output being firmly contracted.</p>
<p>Plant construction began October 1, and is scheduled to be completed on May 31, 1998.</p>
<p>AES currently owns or has an interest in 33 power facilities totaling over 11,000 megawatts in the United States, Argentina, Brazil, Pakistan, Hungary, Kazakhstan, China and the United Kingdom.</p>
<p>((--New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1700))</p>
</text>
